    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-general-1-2008-p7.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\((2,1)\\) The square of a real number is always at least 0 , so to have equality we must have \\((x-2 y)^{2}=0\\) and \\((y-1)^{2}=0\\). Then \\(y=1\\) and \\(x=2 y=2\\).",
